Nope; they're a "death by stupidity" threat in certain small easily
identified parts of the game, and that's the difference. It's hard to be
careful all game; it's easy to be careful at very specific times. Lots of
people (like me) accidentally stash WoCancel if they carry them around;
almost anyone can manage the discipline necessary to use one safely at
their stash.

Also, it doesn't take a single screwup.

Screwup one is not having a WoTele, oilskin, AoMB etc., ready before
moving to a position where you can make screwup two.

Screwup two is moving next to water.

Screwup three is not immediately moving away from the water if you have
the opportunity, which you almost certainly do; only 1/10 of successful
hits result in a potential drowning.

Screwup four, if you didn't make screwup one, is to not hit the panic
button.

You must make #2 and one of #1 and #4, and you almost certainly will have
one or more chances to make #3. I.e., it's at least a double screwup death.

I regularly make #1, by the way, but that's OK because I never make #2.
